From 5230f0e65817e2a19399bffc30679aad426472e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: beau4201 <beau.ten.berge@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:47:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] launcher: show the app drawer as category groups

The main list of the phone launcher becomes one container per category (two per row) with the first four apps as themed icons. A tap opens the group as a frosted card in the middle of the display over a blurred, dimmed drawer, with the stock folder timing. Search, the work tab, the taskbar and Private Space are unchanged. New code lives in allapps/category/; resources in their own file.

launcher: fix the drawer groups after the first device round

Add space above each container so the first row clears the clip at the top of the list and a label no longer touches the next container. Start an app from its icon in the open card instead of closing the card first. Use the stock folder icon size in the card and add the grip of the design.

launcher: rebind the drawer groups on every update

A group draws its icons itself and compared equal when only an icon changed, so it kept the icons of its first binding, unthemed and in the default shape. Stock icon items always rebind; a group now does too.

launcher: group every preinstalled app in System

Every preinstalled app goes to the System group whatever category it declares. The fixed per-package groups for Camera, PDF Viewer and Auditor are no longer needed. Nine unit tests; eight mutations of the logic each fail them.

launcher: load the themed icon of a drawer group in the background

A group draws its icons itself. An app whose themed icon is not cached yet, such as a generated one for an app without a monochrome icon, kept its own colours there while the opened card and search showed it themed. The group now asks the icon cache for it, once per binding, as BubbleTextView and the folder preview do.

launcher: fix the opened group in the dark theme and with a large font

The card took its surface from allAppsSurfaceHighest, which stayed light in the dark theme while the text turned light, so title and labels were hard to read. It now uses the surface of the group containers. The icon cells had a fixed height, so a large font let a label touch the icon of the next row; a cell is now at least that height and grows with its label.

launcher: size the cells of the opened group by their label

The wrap_content cells of the previous change got a huge top padding, because BubbleTextView derives it from the height it is given when centerVertically is set. The cells no longer use centerVertically, so each is as tall as its icon and label, with space below.

launcher: fix the drawer groups after a code review

Accessibility: a group counts as a row and an item, and a group row has two columns. The pre-draw listener of the opened card is removed from the observer it was added to and does not open a card that is already closed. The card ignores touches while it opens and closes, announces itself when it is open, clears its blur when it is removed in any way and is never opened twice. The category of a system app is no longer read.

launcher: space the last row of drawer groups like the rows between them

Every group has space above it and none below, so the last row touched the
Private Space header. The groups of the last row now keep the same space
below their label. The row arithmetic is a pure function with a unit test.

launcher: close the opened drawer group when an icon is dragged out

The card stayed open over the home screen after a drag started from one of
its icons. It now listens for the start of a drag and closes, as the stock
icon menu does, and its view is removed when the drag ends.
